\title{discoverHTE: Discover Heterogeneous Effects of Continuous Exposures}
\description{
Estimates exposure-response functions (ERFs), also called causal dose-response curves, for continuous exposures, and discovers interpretable subgroups across which they differ. The ERF is estimated using the doubly robust estimator of Kennedy et al. (2017) \doi{10.1111/rssb.12212}, with the nuisance functionals fit by generalized linear models, generalized additive models for location, scale, and shape, stacked learners, or Bayesian additive regression trees. Recursive partitioning then splits the sample into subgroups that maximize a measure of the difference between their ERFs, producing a tree in which each node carries its own exposure-response curve.
}
